Just some thoughts from my recent game which ended in an ascension.

 - Stormy is the weakest of the major named weapons.  It doesn't do anything
   special to undead and demons.  This is a draw back in hell as it is
   obviously crawling with both.  Therefore all of this talk about making
   it an even less desirable weapon is really unfair.  (My personal favorites
   are Excaliber and Mjollnir).  In fact the one really neat aspect about
   having Stormy (lowering the level of the wizard by repeatedly using a
   stethescope and judiciously hitting him) is greatly reduced.  Now he
   just scoops up a wand of create monster and in three turns you are
   completely surrounded.

 - The way the end levels are set up, they almost necessitate the use of
   a ring of conflict.  I did everything from the quest on with a RoC in
   my possession, but didn't use it until the very end on the Astral Plane.
   I only did this because I had spent a 1/2 hour in the same room hacking
   away (and spell casting, zapping wands, etc.) and didn't make any
   progress.  I think something should be changed so that it requires a
   little more brains and less patience on these levels.

 - On favorite pet names, I generally use Death (dog) and Famine (cat).
   I've been using these two names since just after the release of 3.0j.

 - On character names, I use a mix of favorite and different names.  Some
   of my favorite names are Aramir, Lurcof, Cursag, Taji, and Tanja.
   However, my recent ascension was with Bob the Elf (I figured that this
   one was NOT going to make it).

 - I really like the idea of the quest, however, in the case of the elf
   quest I had already wiped out Ft. Ludious, Medusa, and the Castle levels
   before I was high enough to go on the quest.  By that time it was like 
   a stroll in the park.  In reality I don't think the Elf quest (only one
   I've been on) was any tougher then some of the lower Gnomish mine levels.

 - I think that the light shop in the Gnomish mines should automatically 
   have a minimum of 7 candles.  I also DON'T think there should be any
   in Vlad's tower.

Anyway that's all I have for now,

Jim B.
